=== upper_archivist ===
[PLACEHOLDER] "So you're the carver. Sit, if you like. I only want to ask a few questions." #speaker:archivist
-> END

=== upper_plaque ===
[PLACEHOLDER] Neat rows of marks on a brass plate. Writing. You can't read a word of it.
-> END

=== upper_feast ===
[PLACEHOLDER] A table laden with more food than your street sees in a week.
-> END

=== upper_masterwork ===
[PLACEHOLDER] A flock of carved birds spiralling up a twisting trunk, every feather cut clean. Whoever made this never slipped once.
-> END

=== upper_fountain ===
[PLACEHOLDER] Water lifted by a turning blessing and poured into a carved basin, over and over, for no reason but beauty.
-> END

=== upper_books ===
[PLACEHOLDER] Shelves and shelves of books. Up here, everyone can read.
-> END
